  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Saint Lucia Sustainable Recovery Development Policy Credit</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The development objectives of the Sustainable Recovery Development Policy Credit for Saint Lucia are to: (i) strengthen fiscal revenues and transparency; and (ii) promote green and resilient private sector growth. The operation consists of two complementary pillars: Pillar 1 supports strengthening fiscal revenues and improving transparency by introducing a health and citizen security levy (HCSL) as well as increases to the excise tax on cigarettes. Pillar 2 focuses on promoting green and resilient private sector growth, by supporting climate change mitigation and adaptation as well as reforms to improve the business environment.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The program development objectives are to (i) strengthen fiscal revenues and transparency; and (ii) promote green and resilient private sector growth.</narrative>
  </description>
